timer: debug -- print every timer_list callback about to run

Continuation of the issue #99 investigation (see docs/M5-AP.md and
DEBUG-timer-softirq-snapshot.patch). During the AP-start softirq freeze,
TIMER_SOFTIRQ shows as pending (local_softirq_pending() bit 0x02) with its
kstat_softirqs_cpu() dispatch count frozen -- consistent with something inside
run_timer_softirq()'s per-timer dispatch (call_timer_fn) hanging mid-call and
never returning, freezing the whole softirq's completion.

Every driver-level candidate checked out clean by reading the source:
rtlwifi's one and only timer_list (the 2s watchdog, just queue_delayed_work +
mod_timer, non-blocking), mac80211's sta_cleanup (no-op with zero stations)
and dynamic_ps_timer (just wiphy_work_queue), and the generic netdev TX-hang
watchdog (net/sched/sch_generic.c's netdev_watchdog_up() returns immediately
without arming when ndo_tx_timeout is NULL -- and mac80211's
ieee80211_dataif_ops does not set it). None of them explain a hang.

Rather than keep guessing from source alone, print every timer_list callback
immediately before AND after it runs, gated on the same rtl819x_debug_armed
flag as the timer-ISR probe so it stays silent outside a deliberately armed
test window (write "1" to /proc/rtl819x_debug_arm first). Whichever callback
prints "fn=..." without a matching "returned" line is the one that hung.

Not intended to stay in the tree once the storm is identified.

